# `.env.example` (template — DO NOT add real values)

> **Note:** FinPlan Pro is **offline-first**. There is no `.env` file in this repo, by design. The app does not connect to any external service, has no API keys, no telemetry, and no cloud URLs.
>
> If you fork the app and add a remote backend, drop your env vars here and update `docs/tech-stack.md` and `docs/security-guidelines.md` accordingly.

---

## Sentry (optional, per T-ATL-007 Sentry self-hosted + T-ATL-009 SDK install)

```ini
# Sentry self-hosted DSN — see T-ATL-007 (Docker Compose + R2 archive).
# Get the DSN from your self-hosted Sentry UI:
#   Settings → Projects → [project] → Client Keys (DSN)
# When VITE_SENTRY_DSN is empty/unset, Sentry.init() is skipped
# entirely (per T-ATL-009 SOP). The app remains offline-first by
# default; Sentry activates only when a DSN is provided.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE=
#
# Session Replay privacy (F-0022): masking is UNCONDITIONAL and is NOT
# configurable here. src/sentryReplayConfig.ts always sets maskAllText,
# maskAllInputs and blockAllMedia, masks the financial selectors and
# value-bearing attributes, and never captures network bodies. Privacy of
# ledger data must not depend on a deployment-time variable, so the previous
# SENTRY_REPLAY_MASK_ALL_TEXT / SENTRY_REPLAYS_* entries were removed: no code
# ever read them, and documenting them implied a control that did not exist.
# Sample rates live in src/main.tsx (session 0.0, on-error 1.0).
# To unmask one element deliberately, add data-sentry-unmask to it.
```

## Mock Auth (build-time gate, per T-HEP-021 PRE-PUSH SECURITY REVIEW P0 #4)

```ini
# In dev/staging, set to "true" to use the local mock auth provider
# (no external IdP, no network). In production this MUST be unset
# or set to "false" — the entry point in src/main.tsx will refuse
# to mount if VITE_USE_MOCK_AUTH is "true" in a production build.
VITE_USE_MOCK_AUTH=false
```

## NIM (NVIDIA Inference Microservice, optional, dev only) — REMOVED FROM CLIENT BUNDLE

```ini
# SECURITY FIX (H-04): VITE_NIM_API_KEY must NOT reach the browser bundle.
# In production, proxy NIM through a server endpoint (/api/nim) using
# a server-side env var (NIM_API_KEY, without VITE_ prefix) so the key
# never reaches the client. The variable below is kept empty by design.
# If NIM integration is needed, implement src/services/auth/nimProxy.ts
# and use server-side authentication.
# VITE_NIM_API_KEY=REMOVED_FROM_CLIENT
```

## Build / Bundle

```ini
# Set to "true" to emit bundle-report/stats.html on next `vite build`
ANALYZE=

# Override the default Vite port (5173, strictPort)
PORT=

# Override the default public path for static assets
BASE_URL=/
```

## Feature flags (build-time gates — default behavior is unchanged)

```ini
# Browser beta mode (F-05, solo-dev validation loop). The app is Tauri-first;
# a plain browser renders ONLY when this is "true" or "1" and shows an honest
# data-beta-web marker. Enabling it is NOT a claim that browser/PWA is a
# supported product capability (A-12 stays UNVALIDATED). Leave unset in
# production until the beta launch decision is made.
# VITE_BETA_WEB=false

# Control Plane client (F-04 spike — feature-flagged, NOT wired into any
# screen). Leave unset: the typed command client stays inert.
# VITE_ENABLE_CONTROL_PLANE=false
# VITE_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=https://control-plane.example.com

# Server API base URL (used by pages that talk to a backend; the app is
# offline-first and does not require one).
# VITE_API_URL=
```

## Tauri (optional desktop build)

```ini
# Tauri CLI auto-detects these. Uncomment to override.
# TAURI_DEV_HOST=
# TAURI_DEV_PORT=
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=
```

## Linting / Testing

```ini
# No runtime heap override is needed. The npm test scripts set
# `--max-old-space-size=8192` (8 GiB), which is proven sufficient for the
# full suite. The former 80 GiB value masked a hang fixed in N-0001.
SKIP_HEAP_OVERRIDE=

# Vitest reporter override (default / spec / verbose / json)
VITEST_REPORTER=
```

## Plugin Marketplace (only if self-hosting)

```ini
# URL of a self-hosted plugin marketplace JSON feed (defaults to local /plugins)
# PLUGIN_MARKETPLACE_URL=
```

## Telemetry / Crash Reporting (intentionally NOT included)

```ini
# This project does NOT collect telemetry. Do not add:
#   SENTRY_DSN=
#   POSTHOG_KEY=
#   AMPLITUDE_API_KEY=
# Adding any of the above would violate the offline-first design contract.
```

---

## Verification

```bash
# Confirm no .env is present (should output nothing)
ls -la .env .env.local .env.production 2>/dev/null || echo "OK: no .env files"

# Confirm Vite still builds without env vars
node node_modules/.bin/vite build
```

> ⚠️ **If you add real environment variables**, ensure they are NOT committed. Add `.env*` to `.gitignore` (currently the repo has no `.env*` files, so `.gitignore` is implicit). Update this file and the project docs in the same PR.
